00:51:09.500 --> 00:51:11.869
Now maybe we can have some peace
and quiet for a while, huh?


00:51:12.937 --> 00:51:14.305
I like the sound of that.


00:51:16.374 --> 00:51:17.374
Excuse me.


00:51:22.113 --> 00:51:23.648
Hamish, well done.


00:51:26.117 --> 00:51:27.752
My pleasure.


00:51:27.918 --> 00:51:31.322
I didn't know that Mason guy for long,
but he's starting to get on my nerves.


00:51:32.157 --> 00:51:34.825
I only wish I could have been
there myself to see the fireworks.


00:51:35.626 --> 00:51:37.828
You and I still have
some business to discuss.


00:51:38.196 --> 00:51:39.196
Not now.


00:51:39.630 --> 00:51:41.399
Tonight is for celebrating.


00:51:41.799 --> 00:51:43.834
Maybe for you, but not for me.


00:51:44.402 --> 00:51:46.036
I said not now, Hamish.


00:51:46.837 --> 00:51:49.574
The only reason I decided
to help you is because you


00:51:49.807 --> 00:51:52.377
finally agreed to cough
up the money you owed me.


00:51:53.010 --> 00:51:55.146
Don't make me
repeat myself again.


00:51:56.414 --> 00:51:57.848
Not everyone's scared of you.


00:51:59.650 --> 00:52:00.685
You sure?


00:52:01.419 --> 00:52:03.721
I was just informed by
a very reliable source


00:52:03.921 --> 00:52:06.056
that I am the most
dangerous man in the world.


00:52:07.225 --> 00:52:08.225
Abel!


00:52:09.427 --> 00:52:11.429
My yacht is headed up this way.


00:52:12.263 --> 00:52:15.666
I trust you and Violet will pack your
bags and disembark before it does so.


00:52:20.438 --> 00:52:21.438
Salud.


00:52:22.440 --> 00:52:22.806
Baby


00:52:22.807 --> 00:52:23.807
To you.


00:52:44.562 --> 00:52:47.464
Well, so much for you
not getting in the water.


00:52:47.465 --> 00:52:48.465
Don't say it.


00:52:49.467 --> 00:52:50.601
Not getting in the water.


00:52:50.801 --> 00:52:51.801
And he said it.


00:52:52.203 --> 00:52:53.403
Explosives?


00:52:53.404 --> 00:52:54.448
What are you talking about, explosives?


00:52:54.472 --> 00:52:55.773
I was trying to tell you.


00:52:55.973 --> 00:52:57.908
We've got to get off
this boat fucking now.


00:52:58.309 --> 00:52:59.309
Come on.


00:53:13.658 --> 00:53:15.493
Damn, man,
this water's cold as hell.


00:53:16.227 --> 00:53:17.561
Fuck this bullshit.


00:53:17.562 --> 00:53:19.496
No, no, you guys can't
complain about anything.


00:53:19.497 --> 00:53:20.617
I'm the one without a hoods.


00:53:20.898 --> 00:53:22.766
Hey, what about me?


00:53:22.767 --> 00:53:25.503
No, no, you, you don't get to
complain about anything ever again.


00:53:26.271 --> 00:53:27.504
Get us into this mess.


00:53:27.505 --> 00:53:28.273
Okay, pick it up.


00:53:28.473 --> 00:53:29.606
Let's go.


00:53:29.607 --> 00:53:30.107
You're the one
who didn't want to wetsuit.


00:53:30.608 --> 00:53:31.608
Shut up.


00:53:32.076 --> 00:53:33.077
This shit is heavy.


00:53:33.911 --> 00:53:36.514
Well, shit,
at least we got the painting.


00:54:02.540 --> 00:54:03.540
Hello?


00:54:08.045 --> 00:54:09.045
Mason?


00:54:10.348 --> 00:54:10.781
Mason?


00:54:10.948 --> 00:54:11.948
It's Mason.


00:54:12.550 --> 00:54:13.550
They're alive.


00:54:14.552 --> 00:54:15.552
How?


00:54:16.521 --> 00:54:17.655
Where are you guys?


00:54:21.559 --> 00:54:22.759
We're going to be right there.


00:54:27.365 --> 00:54:28.566
I'm too old for this, Sean.


00:54:31.569 --> 00:54:32.136
Come on.


00:54:32.337 --> 00:54:33.404
Bring it.


00:54:35.573 --> 00:54:36.574
Oh my god, you guys.


00:54:36.741 --> 00:54:37.741
We thought you were dead.


00:54:37.808 --> 00:54:39.142
Let's go.


00:54:39.143 --> 00:54:39.677
I knew you guys would
make it out somehow.


00:54:40.077 --> 00:54:41.077
Hold it man!


00:54:41.712 --> 00:54:42.980
Let's get the fuck out of here!


00:54:43.581 --> 00:54:44.582
Move it out


00:54:44.749 --> 00:54:46.109
We brought you some clothes, guys.


00:54:47.685 --> 00:54:48.685
Fuck


00:54:49.354 --> 00:54:50.354
Hell yeah!


00:55:09.840 --> 00:55:10.840
Mason.


00:55:14.412 --> 00:55:17.614
After that explosion, I just
didn't know if... Come on, you


00:55:17.615 --> 00:55:21.251
didn't think I had anything to
do with that explosion, did you?


00:55:21.752 --> 00:55:22.752
Oh.


00:55:24.589 --> 00:55:26.223
Sean, hi.


00:55:26.424 --> 00:55:27.525
Good to see you, Odessa.


00:55:27.725 --> 00:55:30.795
Sorry to barge in like
this, but are you busy?


00:55:31.396 --> 00:55:32.730
No, no, no, come on in.


00:55:32.930 --> 00:55:34.399
It's more than just us, though.


00:55:38.235 --> 00:55:39.470
Oh, all right.


00:55:39.637 --> 00:55:40.637
Gang's all here.


00:55:40.638 --> 00:55:41.972
Still okay?


00:55:42.607 --> 00:55:43.272
Very good.


00:55:43.273 --> 00:55:44.273
-Come on.
-Thank you


00:55:48.779 --> 00:55:49.779
Hey.


00:55:51.048 --> 00:55:52.048
Uh-huh


00:56:01.158 --> 00:56:02.158
Come on in.


00:56:06.997 --> 00:56:08.833
We need your opinion
on something.


00:56:11.301 --> 00:56:14.605
Interesting way to spend
your vacation, I see.


00:56:14.772 --> 00:56:15.772
This one's not on me.


00:56:16.006 --> 00:56:17.808
It was my fault, as usual.


00:56:18.609 --> 00:56:21.612
But I think we have something
pretty special on the hands.


00:56:21.779 --> 00:56:22.779
Exciting.


00:56:23.681 --> 00:56:24.681
So?


00:56:36.661 --> 00:56:38.463
Silent Beauty by Winston Penn.


00:56:38.696 --> 00:56:41.699
Currently valued just
north of $100 million.


00:56:41.999 --> 00:56:42.999
$100 million?


00:56:43.434 --> 00:56:44.033
Woo!


00:56:44.034 --> 00:56:44.701
Ok.


00:56:44.702 --> 00:56:46.504
Nicely done, Sean.


00:56:46.704 --> 00:56:47.337
You're tight too, huh?


00:56:47.705 --> 00:56:49.173
Let's put it over here.


00:56:50.207 --> 00:56:52.709
What kind of a fucking idiot would
spend $100 million on this shit?


00:56:52.710 --> 00:56:53.844
This is ugly as fuck.


00:56:54.311 --> 00:56:55.311
I don't know.


00:56:55.546 --> 00:56:57.047
I mean, it sure look good to me.


00:56:57.281 --> 00:56:58.281
Careful.


00:57:11.829 --> 00:57:17.234
I know my methods might be a little crazy
sometimes, but your boy Sean gets it done.


00:57:17.535 --> 00:57:18.002
Yes, sir.


00:57:18.469 --> 00:57:19.737
4D chess, Mason.


00:57:22.139 --> 00:57:23.741
Oh, it's impressive.


00:57:24.675 --> 00:57:25.374
See?


00:57:25.375 --> 00:57:26.375
My girl Odessa gets it.


00:57:26.511 --> 00:57:27.511
Let her finish.


00:57:27.878 --> 00:57:28.745
Yeah.


00:57:28.746 --> 00:57:29.847
Very impressive.


00:57:31.916 --> 00:57:33.751
Impressive... forgery.


00:57:35.185 --> 00:57:36.185
What?


00:57:36.721 --> 00:57:37.961
Wait, you gotta be shitting me.


00:57:39.189 --> 00:57:40.189
No, I don't.


00:57:40.758 --> 00:57:41.424
Sean!


00:57:41.425 --> 00:57:42.759
Don't be shitting me.


00:57:42.760 --> 00:57:43.761
No, it can't be.


00:57:44.361 --> 00:57:44.862
Yeah.


00:57:45.029 --> 00:57:46.029
What do you mean?


00:57:46.163 --> 00:57:46.764
Look at it, Sean.


00:57:46.997 --> 00:57:47.998
It's too perfect.


00:57:48.332 --> 00:57:49.533
See this?


00:57:49.534 --> 00:57:50.734
Take a look
at this section right there.


00:57:50.735 --> 00:57:52.702
You see that?


00:57:52.703 --> 00:57:56.541
In the original painting, you could
see tiny little cracks in the oil paint.


00:57:57.274 --> 00:57:58.274
Come, take a look.


00:57:58.408 --> 00:57:58.943
See that?


00:57:59.276 --> 00:58:00.410
Tough break, Sean.


00:58:00.611 --> 00:58:01.078
Yeah, man.


00:58:01.546 --> 00:58:02.546
Yep.


00:58:03.748 --> 00:58:04.782
Put it, a tough break.


00:58:07.918 --> 00:58:09.886
Hold on.


00:58:09.887 --> 00:58:12.790
So you mean to tell me we almost
got blown up over a fake painting?


00:58:12.957 --> 00:58:14.290
I knew it.


00:58:14.291 --> 00:58:16.131
When that boat blew
up, I knew it was a forger.


00:58:16.527 --> 00:58:16.894
You did?


00:58:17.094 --> 00:58:18.094
Yes, yes.


00:58:18.228 --> 00:58:19.564
That was the plan all the time.


00:58:19.797 --> 00:58:21.430
Don't you get it?


00:58:21.431 --> 00:58:23.801
They wanted to blow us up
and the painting and then collect.


00:58:24.535 --> 00:58:26.737
Who would benefit
from collecting on this?


00:58:27.572 --> 00:58:28.572
Who?


00:58:29.974 --> 00:58:31.641
The owner of the painting.


00:58:31.642 --> 00:58:32.408
That's right.


00:58:32.409 --> 00:58:33.810
It's an insurance scam.


00:58:33.811 --> 00:58:34.812
Bingo.


00:58:35.045 --> 00:58:36.814
Gotta admit,
it's not a bad scheme.


00:58:38.448 --> 00:58:39.983
I think I get it.


00:58:39.984 --> 00:58:42.144
Hey, why don't you spell it
out for us dumb fucks then?


00:58:42.252 --> 00:58:43.252
It's simple.


00:58:43.287 --> 00:58:44.822
Someone buys
an original painting.


00:58:44.989 --> 00:58:46.590
They insure it.


00:58:46.591 --> 00:58:49.259
And if it gets destroyed or
soiled or lost, full recovery.


00:58:49.459 --> 00:58:50.728
You collect everything back.


00:58:50.961 --> 00:58:54.331
All while secretly holding
on to the original painting.


00:58:54.565 --> 00:58:56.567
Yeah, I gotta admit,
that's pretty smart.


00:58:56.934 --> 00:58:58.235
No, it's not that fucking smart.


00:58:58.468 --> 00:59:00.837
If the plan worked and the
word got out, that fuckboy


00:59:00.838 --> 00:59:03.240
Hamish would be on the
hook for four counts of murder.


00:59:04.842 --> 00:59:06.082
You talking about Hamish Hawks?


00:59:07.845 --> 00:59:08.612
Yeah.


00:59:08.613 --> 00:59:09.847
He, uh, he owns the painting.


00:59:10.014 --> 00:59:11.849
Hamish Hawks doesn't own
Silent Beauty.


00:59:12.249 --> 00:59:13.249
You sure?


00:59:13.851 --> 00:59:14.851
It was on his yacht.


00:59:15.653 --> 00:59:17.487
That's not Hamish's yacht.


00:59:17.955 --> 00:59:19.857
It belongs to one of
his business associates.


00:59:20.490 --> 00:59:21.858
No, no, no.


00:59:21.859 --> 00:59:23.027
That's why Richter's here.


00:59:25.095 --> 00:59:26.263
Hell fucking no.


00:59:27.665 --> 00:59:29.625
Please don't say what I
think you're about to say.


00:59:30.635 --> 00:59:33.003
Salzar owns the painting
and the yacht.


00:59:33.203 --> 00:59:34.271
Is that right?


00:59:34.471 --> 00:59:37.173
Well, technically, the
painting and the yacht


00:59:37.174 --> 00:59:40.177
are listed under a couple
of his shell companies.


00:59:40.377 --> 00:59:41.577
But yeah, Mason, you're right.


00:59:41.846 --> 00:59:42.846
It's Salsar.


00:59:43.814 --> 00:59:45.449
How can you be so sure?


00:59:45.883 --> 00:59:50.154
Because I'm the one that brokered the
deal back when he bought the painting.


00:59:52.657 --> 00:59:56.226
Abel Salzar is my client.


00:59:57.895 --> 00:59:58.262
Oh.


00:59:58.462 --> 00:59:59.028
Oh, shit.


00:59:59.029 --> 01:00:00.297
Oh, hell no.


01:00:07.872 --> 01:00:08.906
Can I try some?


01:00:09.073 --> 01:00:09.873
No.


01:00:09.874 --> 01:00:11.340
You have your own ice cream.


01:00:11.341 --> 01:00:12.341
Whatever.


01:00:16.213 --> 01:00:17.547
What's the matter,
Agent Richter?


01:00:18.916 --> 01:00:19.917
No ice cream for you?


01:00:20.918 --> 01:00:22.152
I'm lactose intolerant.


01:00:24.321 --> 01:00:26.056
You don't seem surprised
to see me.


01:00:26.924 --> 01:00:29.684
You don't really think I thought
that you were killed in an explosion.


01:00:30.094 --> 01:00:31.328
You played that trick before.


01:00:32.062 --> 01:00:33.563
Well, this one's not on me, man.


01:00:34.865 --> 01:00:37.267
Maybe it was Decker trying
to put you out of your misery.


01:00:38.568 --> 01:00:40.569
I tell you, I'm sorry to
hear the two of you broke


01:00:40.570 --> 01:00:42.372
up, but I could have
told you a long time ago.


01:00:42.940 --> 01:00:43.941
It was never gonna last.


01:00:44.574 --> 01:00:45.574
Well, you didn't.


01:00:45.943 --> 01:00:47.712
I'm always the last to know,
aren't I?


01:00:48.378 --> 01:00:49.978
You think maybe I have a chance
with her?


01:00:51.581 --> 01:00:53.951
You love to see me in
a tight spot, don't you?


01:00:55.252 --> 01:00:56.921
I'd say I'm entitled
to gloat a little.


01:00:57.354 --> 01:00:59.354
How many times have I
had to chase you in the past?


01:00:59.957 --> 01:01:01.290
Now you're coming to me.


01:01:01.291 --> 01:01:03.961
I would have appreciated
a heads-up once also.


01:01:04.461 --> 01:01:05.763
Now, why would I do that?


01:01:06.296 --> 01:01:08.065
I can just trail
your crew instead.


01:01:08.966 --> 01:01:11.802
Oh, so you admit it,
that you use us as bait.


01:01:12.737 --> 01:01:14.271
I admit to being good
at what I do.


01:01:18.275 --> 01:01:19.275
So where is he?


01:01:19.810 --> 01:01:20.810
Where's Salzar?


01:01:25.282 --> 01:01:26.115
Hm?


01:01:26.116 --> 01:01:27.116
You don't know, do you?


01:01:28.285 --> 01:01:29.953
Oh, my god.


01:01:29.954 --> 01:01:32.394
You almost get us killed, and
you don't even know where he is.


01:01:32.957 --> 01:01:34.677
Maybe you're not as
good as you say you are.


01:01:34.925 --> 01:01:36.125
Yeah, well, he's not an idiot.


01:01:36.160 --> 01:01:37.640
And I know he's
around here somewhere.


01:01:37.995 --> 01:01:39.996
But he uses proxies
for everything.


01:01:39.997 --> 01:01:41.598
His proxies have proxies.


01:01:41.999 --> 01:01:42.999
The man's a ghost.


01:01:44.001 --> 01:01:45.635
And now he thinks I'm a ghost, so.


01:01:46.003 --> 01:01:47.003
Well, lucky for you.


01:01:47.171 --> 01:01:48.839
No, unlucky for him.


01:01:49.006 --> 01:01:50.007
I'm tired of this shit.


01:01:51.776 --> 01:01:52.776
We've gotten him before.


01:01:53.010 --> 01:01:54.010
We'll get him again.


01:01:54.178 --> 01:01:54.845
What are you saying?


01:01:55.012 --> 01:01:55.746
You have a plan?


01:01:56.013 --> 01:01:57.013
I do.


01:01:58.415 --> 01:01:59.415
I think I do.


01:02:00.317 --> 01:02:01.317
Tell me more.


01:02:27.778 --> 01:02:30.547
I think that was the best
pasta I've ever tasted.


01:02:31.215 --> 01:02:31.848
No, really


01:02:31.849 --> 01:02:33.050
Well, thank you.


01:02:33.383 --> 01:02:35.052
How do you do that?


01:02:35.219 --> 01:02:39.556
Well, actually, I used to go out with
one of the biggest chefs in the world.


01:02:39.790 --> 01:02:40.891
You've seen him on TV.


01:02:41.058 --> 01:02:43.060
And I picked up a few skills.


01:02:43.460 --> 01:02:44.393
That makes sense.


01:02:44.394 --> 01:02:46.831
Before, I caught him in bed with


01:02:47.631 --> 01:02:50.066
an Academy Award
winning actress.


01:02:50.067 --> 01:02:51.067
I'm sorry.


01:02:53.203 --> 01:02:54.204
Don't be.


01:02:54.571 --> 01:02:58.508
I'm enjoying taking time just
for myself.


01:03:00.044 --> 01:03:01.378
You know?


01:03:01.545 --> 01:03:04.681
It can get lonely, but everybody
gets a little lonely sometimes.


01:03:06.216 --> 01:03:08.252
Probably even someone
like Abel Salazar.


01:03:10.687 --> 01:03:12.389
How long have you been working
with him?


01:03:13.090 --> 01:03:17.394
Well, his people used to buy some of
the art I stole back when I was a thief.


01:03:18.695 --> 01:03:21.731
And once I went legit, I did
some business with Hamish,


01:03:21.932 --> 01:03:24.835
but then I realized that
Hamish was just the middleman.


01:03:25.102 --> 01:03:26.603
Salazar was the real buyer.


01:03:26.904 --> 01:03:32.075
Eventually, Abel came to trust
me enough to work with me directly.


01:03:32.076 --> 01:03:34.711
You should be careful with him.


01:03:36.113 --> 01:03:41.418
I know he's suave and sophisticated
and all that, but he's a bad man.


01:03:42.519 --> 01:03:43.854
I can take care of myself.


01:03:44.121 --> 01:03:45.754
I know you can.


01:03:45.755 --> 01:03:48.235
I just wouldn't want to see
anything happen to you, that's all.


01:03:49.126 --> 01:03:50.126
Why?


01:03:51.128 --> 01:03:52.128
Because I care.


01:03:52.897 --> 01:03:53.897
I care about you.


01:03:57.134 --> 01:03:58.134
Mason.


01:03:59.136 --> 01:04:00.871
We should talk more
about this plan.


01:04:02.539 --> 01:04:03.539
The plan, Mason?


01:04:03.707 --> 01:04:05.774
We've gone
over it half a dozen times.


01:04:05.775 --> 01:04:08.378
Yeah, but we don't have a
plan B, and that's important.


01:04:08.645 --> 01:04:12.316
With a plan A that's good, you don't
need a plan B. I don't know about that.


01:04:12.950 --> 01:04:15.452
Mason, we've got this.


01:04:17.922 --> 01:04:20.891
Okay, well,
I should go check on the crew.


01:04:22.326 --> 01:04:24.895
Make sure that Sean
doesn't get in trouble.


01:04:26.663 --> 01:04:27.731
He's lucky to have you.


01:04:27.932 --> 01:04:28.932
They all are.


01:04:29.499 --> 01:04:30.800
I feel the same way about them.


01:04:31.801 --> 01:04:34.138
You know, they drive me a
little crazy, but I feel happy.


01:04:34.304 --> 01:04:35.539
Family.


01:04:36.473 --> 01:04:37.473
Good night.


01:04:41.912 --> 01:04:42.912
Good night, Mace.


01:04:43.180 --> 01:04:44.180
French way.


01:04:52.589 --> 01:04:53.589
Oh, my God.


01:04:53.790 --> 01:04:54.423
So decadent.


01:04:54.424 --> 01:04:55.424
I love it.


01:04:55.692 --> 01:04:56.759
You finish it.


01:04:56.760 --> 01:04:58.094
I'm stuffed.


01:04:58.095 --> 01:04:59.975
Oh, are you sure I'm not
getting too much sugar?


01:05:00.931 --> 01:05:02.632
That was a pretty good line, huh?


01:05:03.200 --> 01:05:05.202
You're very convincing baby.


01:05:06.003 --> 01:05:07.204
It's what I do.


01:05:07.771 --> 01:05:10.207
I knew he didn't like
bullies, so I played the bully.


01:05:11.508 --> 01:05:14.211
It gave him a little bit more
incentive to want to steal from me.


01:05:15.545 --> 01:05:17.948
Or at least to think it was
you he was stealing from.


01:05:18.148 --> 01:05:19.148
That's right.


01:05:19.716 --> 01:05:21.218
I knew he wouldn't be able
to resist.


01:05:22.652 --> 01:05:25.789
Well, you are irresistible.


01:05:27.024 --> 01:05:28.525
Even more so than this cake.


01:05:48.678 --> 01:05:49.046
Hey.


01:05:49.346 --> 01:05:50.346
Hey.


01:05:50.480 --> 01:05:51.081
How was dinner?


01:05:51.248 --> 01:05:52.416
It was good.


01:05:53.183 --> 01:05:55.263
Yeah, I told Odessa it was
the best pasta I ever had.


01:05:56.053 --> 01:06:01.690
Some sort of, like, lobster,
scallops, and, like, a fettuccine type.


01:06:01.691 --> 01:06:02.691
It was good.


01:06:06.563 --> 01:06:08.265
You know, she still likes you.


01:06:10.700 --> 01:06:12.660
She didn't invite any of
the rest of us to dinner.


01:06:13.037 --> 01:06:14.717
Well, that's because
we had to make a plan.


01:06:15.572 --> 01:06:16.773
Sure, the plan.


01:06:17.274 --> 01:06:18.274
Mm-hmm.


01:06:20.077 --> 01:06:21.077
Do you trust her?


01:06:25.049 --> 01:06:25.482
Yeah.


01:06:25.715 --> 01:06:26.715
Yeah, I do.


01:06:28.252 --> 01:06:29.252
Good.


01:06:32.789 --> 01:06:35.025
You know, it's... it's okay.


01:06:36.226 --> 01:06:38.062
What's okay?


01:06:38.295 --> 01:06:45.035
I mean, not to sound cheesy about it, but,
like, it's okay to open your heart back up.


01:06:48.805 --> 01:06:49.438
Uh...


01:06:49.439 --> 01:06:50.439
My sweet brother.


01:06:51.308 --> 01:06:51.975
Wow.


01:06:52.309 --> 01:06:53.309
You're a good man.


01:06:54.311 --> 01:06:55.312
So are you, Mason.


01:06:57.114 --> 01:06:58.114
Yeah.


01:07:01.285 --> 01:07:02.365
It's getting cold out here.


01:07:03.887 --> 01:07:04.988
You come back inside?


01:07:06.123 --> 01:07:08.558
No, I'm gonna wait
till the roaches vacate.


01:07:09.326 --> 01:07:10.926
Then I'll go back in.


01:07:10.927 --> 01:07:13.247
Yeah, this is definitely a step
down from that resort, huh?


01:07:22.906 --> 01:07:25.175
Odessa, how did the auction go?


01:07:26.276 --> 01:07:27.276
Excellent.


01:07:27.277 --> 01:07:29.179
I got you every piece
you wanted.


01:07:30.347 --> 01:07:31.348
Of course you did.


01:07:31.748 --> 01:07:33.083
That's why I pay you so well.


01:07:33.983 --> 01:07:35.919
I'll have them all
delivered to you tomorrow.


01:07:36.353 --> 01:07:40.357
And I was thinking I might make the
drive up and see you and Hector as well.


01:07:41.458 --> 01:07:43.593
Oh, and to what would we owe
that honor?


01:07:44.594 --> 01:07:45.995
I have a surprise for you.


01:07:47.364 --> 01:07:48.764
What is it with women
and surprises?


01:07:48.932 --> 01:07:51.868
It's about Mason Goddard.


01:07:52.369 --> 01:07:53.670
Yes, I know.


01:07:53.870 --> 01:07:55.371
Mason Goddard, he's dead.


01:07:55.372 --> 01:07:56.372
He's fish food.


01:07:57.707 --> 01:07:58.508
No, Abel.


01:07:58.708 --> 01:08:00.110
Mason is alive.


01:08:01.311 --> 01:08:03.313
And he's going to make
a move against you.


01:08:04.881 --> 01:08:07.784
And I know exactly
what he's planning to do.


01:08:24.568 --> 01:08:25.768
Please open your trunk, ma'am.


01:08:26.336 --> 01:08:27.336
Sure.


01:08:36.413 --> 01:08:37.413
We're clear.


01:08:41.218 --> 01:08:42.218
Welcome, ma'am.


01:08:42.419 --> 01:08:43.986
Thank you.


01:08:43.987 --> 01:08:46.227
The truck with the new
artwork will be following shortly.


01:08:46.823 --> 01:08:47.823
All right, thanks.


01:09:10.847 --> 01:09:12.782
I'm going to have to frisk you.


01:09:13.016 --> 01:09:14.751
Well, have at it, handsome.


01:09:14.951 --> 01:09:17.053
Although I don't know
where I'd be hiding anything.


01:09:17.687 --> 01:09:19.356
That won't be necessary.


01:09:19.623 --> 01:09:23.293
Odessa will never hurt me, because
that would be very bad for business.


01:09:25.462 --> 01:09:27.463
I might try to steal from you.


01:09:27.464 --> 01:09:29.298
Oh, my god.


01:09:29.299 --> 01:09:31.939
Your commissions on these deals
are already grand larceny, my dear.


01:09:32.269 --> 01:09:34.237
You know I'm worth it.


01:09:34.238 --> 01:09:35.472
Oh, you definitely are.


01:09:36.573 --> 01:09:38.608
So you noticed the new
landscaping, right?


01:09:39.209 --> 01:09:40.569
Well, yeah,
I did. You have like...


01:09:40.910 --> 01:09:42.245
A park in front of your house.


01:09:42.246 --> 01:09:42.912
It's beautiful, right?


01:09:43.213 --> 01:09:44.213
Yeah.


01:09:44.981 --> 01:09:46.082
So, what do you think?


01:09:48.051 --> 01:09:50.587
Oh, cute little place
you got here, Abel.


01:09:50.787 --> 01:09:51.787
My humble abode.


01:09:52.656 --> 01:09:53.656
Where's the restroom?


01:09:53.723 --> 01:09:55.225
Right down the hall on the left.


01:09:55.625 --> 01:09:56.759
Thank you.


01:09:56.760 --> 01:09:57.494
I'll wait
for you in the brain room.


01:09:57.727 --> 01:09:58.727
All right.


01:10:03.600 --> 01:10:10.139
Bold move to so prominently display a
supposedly destroyed work of art, Abel.


01:10:14.911 --> 01:10:16.280
Your collection has grown.


01:10:16.913 --> 01:10:17.913
Yeah.


01:10:20.517 --> 01:10:21.517
Interesting.


01:10:22.686 --> 01:10:24.153
That is Alex.


01:10:26.523 --> 01:10:28.492
You name your guns?


01:10:29.526 --> 01:10:31.528
Well, that one has a
special meaning to me.


01:10:33.129 --> 01:10:34.531
You consider this a piece
of art?


01:10:35.532 --> 01:10:36.633
Why not?


01:10:38.535 --> 01:10:41.538
But don't touch it,
because that is a real gun.


01:10:44.774 --> 01:10:45.774
Is it loaded?


01:10:47.877 --> 01:10:48.878
Of course it is.


01:10:50.380 --> 01:10:52.649
An unloaded weapon
is like a blank canvas.


01:10:53.517 --> 01:10:57.186
Useful to the artist, but of
no use to a collector like me.


01:10:58.655 --> 01:10:59.856
Can I offer you champagne?


01:11:00.056 --> 01:11:01.558
Well, I never say no to bubbly.


01:11:02.859 --> 01:11:05.128
Nectar, Odessa is here.


01:11:12.669 --> 01:11:14.170
Odessa.


01:11:14.371 --> 01:11:15.003
Hello.


01:11:15.004 --> 01:11:15.605
Love the outfit.


01:11:15.805 --> 01:11:17.574
Oh, right back at you.


01:11:17.874 --> 01:11:18.874
So good to see you.


01:11:19.008 --> 01:11:19.675
Yeah?


01:11:19.676 --> 01:11:20.108
You look amazing.


01:11:20.109 --> 01:11:20.744
How are you?


01:11:21.077 --> 01:11:22.077
Everything's wonderful.


01:11:22.412 --> 01:11:23.479
Good.


01:11:23.480 --> 01:11:25.349
So happy we... I know,
we did it.


01:11:25.549 --> 01:11:27.083
Sweetheart, right on time.


01:11:28.585 --> 01:11:30.520
So, what are we celebrating?


01:11:31.321 --> 01:11:33.590
Well, to fine art.


01:11:33.823 --> 01:11:35.191
I like that.


01:11:35.592 --> 01:11:37.927
Here's to owning art the
whole world thinks has been lost.


01:11:38.928 --> 01:11:39.928
How about...


01:11:40.930 --> 01:11:43.600
to owning the entire world.


01:11:45.402 --> 01:11:46.436
Salud.


01:11:46.936 --> 01:11:47.936
Cheers.


01:14:16.486 --> 01:14:17.554
We've been expecting you.


01:14:24.728 --> 01:14:25.728
Clear!


01:15:21.585 --> 01:15:23.265
Sean got caught before
I could pick him up.


01:15:24.654 --> 01:15:25.654
Damn it.


01:15:33.129 --> 01:15:34.129
Be careful, babe.


01:15:46.409 --> 01:15:49.679
Gentlemen, please
unload the crates over here.


01:15:51.581 --> 01:15:52.849
And give them a hand, please.


01:16:00.824 --> 01:16:02.091
Right over here, please.


01:16:04.594 --> 01:16:05.795
This is exciting.


01:16:16.172 --> 01:16:18.007
A gift from me to you, Abel.


01:16:18.875 --> 01:16:20.610
Abel does not like surprises.


01:16:20.877 --> 01:16:23.111
Well, this is no surprise,
Nectar.


01:16:23.112 --> 01:16:24.881
Odessa gave me
a heads-up last night.


01:16:25.481 --> 01:16:26.214
Oh?


01:16:26.215 --> 01:16:27.215
What is it?


01:16:27.283 --> 01:16:28.283
Open it!


01:16:39.696 --> 01:16:40.897
Bravo!


01:16:42.632 --> 01:16:46.836
Just like Lazarus, Mason
God arises from the dead.


01:16:48.905 --> 01:16:50.238
How?


01:16:50.239 --> 01:16:52.909
Well, vermin are notoriously
difficult to exterminate.


01:16:53.409 --> 01:16:55.411
Yeah,
it can be hard to kill a rat.


01:16:55.912 --> 01:16:56.913
Mm-hmm.


01:16:57.146 --> 01:16:59.348
Well, maybe this was
meant to be, baby.


01:17:00.316 --> 01:17:01.918
You regretted Mason
didn't suffer more?


01:17:02.719 --> 01:17:03.719
Well, that's right.


01:17:03.920 --> 01:17:05.521
Now we have the chance
to fix that.


01:17:06.723 --> 01:17:08.057
You know,
Mason and I go way back.


01:17:08.925 --> 01:17:12.561
We once even competed to steal
the same Giacometti sculpture.


01:17:12.929 --> 01:17:14.163
And he won that little game.


01:17:14.864 --> 01:17:17.100
But now I win
a much bigger game.


01:17:18.668 --> 01:17:19.668
Really?


01:17:20.704 --> 01:17:22.338
I was just a game to you, huh,
Odessa?


01:17:24.240 --> 01:17:27.176
He thought that I would
help him steal from you.


01:17:27.944 --> 01:17:28.544
Oh.


01:17:28.945 --> 01:17:29.979
So what was the plan?


01:17:30.513 --> 01:17:32.948
Sneak into my villa, make
away with some of my


01:17:32.949 --> 01:17:35.584
valuables, and what,
drive off into the sunset?


01:17:37.386 --> 01:17:40.289
Well, when you say it like that,
it sounds pretty simple, but...


01:17:41.290 --> 01:17:43.526
Yeah, I guess that was the plan.


01:17:44.961 --> 01:17:45.961
You trust her?


01:17:47.964 --> 01:17:48.964
Thanks, Odessa.


01:17:49.065 --> 01:17:50.433
Best gift ever.


01:17:51.600 --> 01:17:54.470
Well, to be fair, it is a gift I
expect to be compensated for.


01:17:54.704 --> 01:17:56.572
Oh, you will be, I promise.


01:17:57.974 --> 01:18:01.978
Just curious, Odessa, how
much is my life worth to you?


01:18:02.946 --> 01:18:03.980
What's the number?


01:18:06.382 --> 01:18:07.984
Probably not as
much as you think.


01:18:12.221 --> 01:18:16.559
Did you really think I was going
to let you rip off my biggest client?


01:18:17.126 --> 01:18:19.729
Because once upon a time, you
used to mean something to me.


01:18:20.997 --> 01:18:21.998
Yeah, I guess I did.


01:18:26.635 --> 01:18:28.772
First Decker, now this.


01:18:29.638 --> 01:18:31.507
You have terrible luck
with women, Mason.


01:18:32.976 --> 01:18:33.976
Maybe I do.


01:18:34.410 --> 01:18:36.512
And I almost feel sorry for you.


01:18:39.015 --> 01:18:40.015
I guess it's a...


01:18:42.018 --> 01:18:45.021
-There's always plan B.
-Plan B?


01:18:53.029 --> 01:18:53.662
Where is he?


01:18:54.030 --> 01:18:55.331
No, no, no, no, no, no.


01:18:55.531 --> 01:18:56.531
Go find him!


01:22:04.053 --> 01:22:05.053
You ready, babe?


01:22:05.221 --> 01:22:06.221
On your word, honey.


01:22:21.237 --> 01:22:22.237
Now!


01:22:22.571 --> 01:22:23.639
Fire in the hole.


01:22:42.658 --> 01:22:43.658
Son of a bitch.


01:22:44.660 --> 01:22:45.260
It's okay, baby.


01:22:45.261 --> 01:22:46.061
Hey, it's okay.


01:22:46.062 --> 01:22:47.262
Somebody's gonna pay for this.


01:22:47.430 --> 01:22:48.998
It's okay.


01:22:52.268 --> 01:22:52.601
Move.


01:22:53.269 --> 01:22:54.269
Move?


01:22:55.071 --> 01:22:56.071
Jeez.


01:22:59.275 --> 01:23:00.843
You need to chill out, bro.


01:23:01.277 --> 01:23:03.246
Maybe you should try
some CBD gummies.


01:23:03.879 --> 01:23:07.050
Maybe you should stay off
yachts where you're not welcome.


01:23:11.387 --> 01:23:12.888
What the fuck, Odessa?


01:23:13.289 --> 01:23:14.590
Hey, I did my part.


01:23:14.790 --> 01:23:15.857
I delivered him to you.


01:23:15.858 --> 01:23:17.298
I'm not the one
who let him get away.


01:23:17.793 --> 01:23:19.313
You can always get
another yacht, baby.


01:23:19.462 --> 01:23:21.064
Maybe even a bigger one.


01:23:21.797 --> 01:23:24.267
Hey, this is the guy
who blew up your yacht.


01:23:28.537 --> 01:23:29.537
Where's Mason?


01:23:30.273 --> 01:23:30.906
I don't know, sir.


01:23:31.107 --> 01:23:32.107
Then go find him!


01:23:38.647 --> 01:23:40.649
Why the fuck would
you blow up my yacht?


01:23:42.251 --> 01:23:43.286
Oh, my God.


01:23:45.288 --> 01:23:46.968
You still haven't
figured it out, have you?


01:23:47.056 --> 01:23:48.056
Hands up now?


01:23:51.427 --> 01:23:52.427
You got me.


01:23:52.928 --> 01:23:53.928
Weapon.


01:24:00.636 --> 01:24:01.636
Why would you come back?


01:24:02.171 --> 01:24:03.731
I thought your brother
was the dumb one.


01:24:05.308 --> 01:24:07.188
My brother's a lot of
things, but he's not dumb.


01:24:08.344 --> 01:24:08.944
You know what?


01:24:09.345 --> 01:24:10.479
Thank you, Mason.


01:24:11.114 --> 01:24:13.149
What is it exactly that I
haven't figured out yet?


01:24:13.349 --> 01:24:15.151
Sean, do the honors.


01:24:16.652 --> 01:24:18.087
You ever heard of 4D chess?


01:24:19.088 --> 01:24:20.356
Oh, Jesus Christ.


01:24:21.457 --> 01:24:23.359
Mason wasn't the only one
in those crates.


01:24:33.369 --> 01:24:36.372
So Anton and the new
guy are here somewhere.


01:24:37.306 --> 01:24:38.473
Perfect.


01:24:38.474 --> 01:24:41.677
Manme will find them,
and you can all die together.


01:24:46.182 --> 01:24:46.981
Sweet Link.


01:24:46.982 --> 01:24:48.516
Let's get this shit.


01:24:48.517 --> 01:24:50.195
Hey, hey, you just make
sure you hold on right there.


01:24:50.219 --> 01:24:51.579
Let's get the fuck out
of here now.


01:24:58.794 --> 01:24:59.794
So what?


01:25:03.832 --> 01:25:05.400
So now you steal my car?


01:25:05.401 --> 01:25:06.635
I'm supposed to be impressed.


01:25:06.835 --> 01:25:07.970
They have dozens of them.


01:25:08.171 --> 01:25:11.039
Yeah, well, auto theft,
it's not our strong suit.


01:25:13.809 --> 01:25:14.809
You.


01:25:15.344 --> 01:25:16.344
You're part of this.


01:25:17.012 --> 01:25:18.012
Who, me?


01:25:19.415 --> 01:25:19.782
Yeah.


01:25:20.416 --> 01:25:21.417
Oh, shit.


01:25:22.151 --> 01:25:23.652
I knew I was forgetting
something.


01:25:23.986 --> 01:25:24.653
No, you're doing good.


01:25:24.853 --> 01:25:26.988
You're good.


01:25:26.989 --> 01:25:30.426
I mean, didn't you wonder how Mason
was able to start that boat so quickly?


01:25:31.660 --> 01:25:33.300
Hey, cute little place
you got here, Abel.


01:25:33.396 --> 01:25:34.396
My humble abode.


01:25:34.530 --> 01:25:36.064
Where's the restroom?


01:25:36.432 --> 01:25:37.712
Right down the hall on the left.


01:25:38.267 --> 01:25:39.401
Thank you.


01:25:39.402 --> 01:25:40.412
I'll wait
for you in the break room.


01:25:40.436 --> 01:25:41.436
All right.


01:26:03.459 --> 01:26:05.460
I don't understand boats,
but that does sound like


01:26:05.461 --> 01:26:07.381
something that should
have occurred to you, Abel.


01:26:07.563 --> 01:26:08.696
I'm just saying.


01:26:08.697 --> 01:26:10.565
Yeah, yeah, yeah.


01:26:10.566 --> 01:26:12.844
And while all that was happening,
I was sneaking out of the yacht.


01:26:12.868 --> 01:26:13.868
All stealthy.


01:26:14.270 --> 01:26:15.270
Like a badass.


01:26:15.871 --> 01:26:17.373
Like a ninja.


01:26:19.708 --> 01:26:22.778
And not that you would
care, Salazar, but don't worry.


01:26:22.978 --> 01:26:25.618
Link made sure the whole crew
was safe before we blew up the yacht.


01:26:26.315 --> 01:26:27.626
She made a little
call this morning.


01:26:27.650 --> 01:26:29.150
Yes, Captain.


01:26:29.151 --> 01:26:31.987
This is Suzanne Connors from
Custom Yachts Incorporated.


01:26:32.488 --> 01:26:36.592
I'm afraid we've got a little problem with
a carbon monoxide leak on your vessel.


01:26:37.493 --> 01:26:39.495
You need to evacuate
the crew immediately.


01:26:41.330 --> 01:26:42.598
Yeah, I understand.


01:26:44.467 --> 01:26:47.636
Our technicians are on the
way to fix the issue right now.


01:26:48.237 --> 01:26:50.138
And did you see that explosion?


01:26:52.241 --> 01:26:56.645
It was our best distraction ever, giving
Mason the chance to sneak back here.


01:27:01.950 --> 01:27:04.620
And giving me a chance
to finally blow his brains out.


01:27:04.953 --> 01:27:06.522
May I tell you something?


01:27:07.490 --> 01:27:08.810
Now,
I don't know a lot about art.


01:27:08.924 --> 01:27:10.124
I really don't.


01:27:10.125 --> 01:27:12.861
But I really kind
of like this painting.


01:27:13.095 --> 01:27:13.528
Kind of like it?


01:27:13.529 --> 01:27:14.962
Yes.


01:27:14.963 --> 01:27:17.165
It is worth over $100
million, you fucking idiot.


01:27:17.533 --> 01:27:18.767
That's my point, you see.


01:27:19.535 --> 01:27:22.471
But I do know someone
who knows a lot about art.


01:27:23.306 --> 01:27:25.341
And they say, well, they
say that... Ah, ah, ah.


01:27:26.542 --> 01:27:27.676
Back off.


01:27:28.544 --> 01:27:31.480
Okay, let me tell you
from a distance then, okay?


01:27:31.714 --> 01:27:36.951
If you go to your painting and
you look closely, okay, you'll see


01:27:36.952 --> 01:27:42.157
that the paint strokes are perfect,
but they're too perfect, okay?


01:27:42.391 --> 01:27:45.360
There should be little
cracks in the paint stroke.


01:27:45.361 --> 01:27:45.794
Do you see that?


01:27:46.194 --> 01:27:46.729
There's not.


01:27:47.062 --> 01:27:48.163
In the oil paint.


01:27:49.665 --> 01:27:51.567
So I think you've got
a forger on your hands.


01:27:53.336 --> 01:27:54.537
Yeah.


01:27:55.571 --> 01:27:58.574
Oh, and you know, before
Anton and Victor stole your car,


01:27:58.907 --> 01:28:00.147
They swapped the paintings out.


01:28:10.018 --> 01:28:10.819
Sweet Link!


01:28:11.019 --> 01:28:11.420
Hundred mil!


01:28:11.587 --> 01:28:12.587
Whoo!


01:28:15.724 --> 01:28:17.593
Now you all fucking die.


01:28:24.833 --> 01:28:25.833
Uh-oh.


01:28:26.602 --> 01:28:27.602
You know what?


01:28:28.170 --> 01:28:29.605
I know I forgot one last thing.


01:28:30.906 --> 01:28:32.107
Can I offer you champagne?


01:28:32.575 --> 01:28:33.909
Well, I never say no to bubbly.


01:28:35.411 --> 01:28:37.212
Nectar, Odessa is here.


01:28:52.194 --> 01:28:53.195
Motherfucker.


01:28:56.732 --> 01:28:57.566
Checkmate?


01:28:57.733 --> 01:28:58.133
Nope.


01:28:58.434 --> 01:28:58.801
Not quite.


01:28:59.134 --> 01:29:00.134
Almost.


01:29:23.659 --> 01:29:24.592
Hello, Abel.


01:29:24.593 --> 01:29:25.828
It's nice to see you again.


01:29:28.263 --> 01:29:29.663
Why don't you put
that on the floor?


01:29:33.669 --> 01:29:33.969
Now?


01:29:34.603 --> 01:29:35.603
Now.


01:29:35.904 --> 01:29:37.305
Checkmate, Salazar.


01:29:37.506 --> 01:29:39.975
Oh, for fuck's sake, get me
away from these people, please.


01:29:40.809 --> 01:29:41.809
Please!


01:29:55.190 --> 01:29:56.792
So you're like
the mastermind now?


01:29:57.493 --> 01:29:58.694
I can't keep track of you.


01:30:10.806 --> 01:30:14.142
It looks like my old pal Abel Salazar
is out of the picture once again.


01:30:14.810 --> 01:30:16.512
Creating quite the power vacuum.


01:30:17.480 --> 01:30:19.715
Sounds like a business
opportunity for someone like you.


01:30:20.315 --> 01:30:21.717
Opportunity for us.


01:30:23.719 --> 01:30:25.919
You knew he was still alive
this whole time, didn't you?


01:30:27.222 --> 01:30:29.542
Mason, you never said anything
about blowing up the yachts.


01:30:30.893 --> 01:30:32.528
A yacht blew up?


01:30:32.728 --> 01:30:33.295
Yikes.


01:30:33.496 --> 01:30:34.530
Sounds dangerous.


01:30:34.730 --> 01:30:36.410
Yeah, well,
you're lucky nobody got killed.


01:30:36.832 --> 01:30:38.000
Our deal would have been off.


01:30:39.134 --> 01:30:41.570
Why don't you try keeping
him behind bars this time?


01:30:42.170 --> 01:30:43.650
Do I look like a prison warden
to you?


01:30:43.872 --> 01:30:45.173
My job's just to catch him.


01:30:46.241 --> 01:30:47.743
Well then, well done.


01:30:48.744 --> 01:30:49.744
Thanks.


01:30:50.045 --> 01:30:51.479
Do me a favor.


01:30:51.480 --> 01:30:52.724
Keep that brother of
yours out of trouble, please.


01:30:52.748 --> 01:30:53.828
Oh, I can't guarantee that.


01:30:54.382 --> 01:30:56.160
I'd hate to have to put
him behind bars one day.


01:30:56.184 --> 01:30:57.352
You know I will if I have to.


01:30:57.586 --> 01:30:58.586
Hmm.


01:30:59.488 --> 01:31:00.568
But can you keep him there?


01:31:01.724 --> 01:31:02.724
Ah.


01:31:03.592 --> 01:31:04.592
Let's go.


01:31:05.761 --> 01:31:07.896
I never underestimated
Mason Goddard.


01:31:09.732 --> 01:31:10.933
But Abel Salazar sure did.


01:31:12.501 --> 01:31:14.770
You know who else Abel
Salazar underestimated?


01:31:16.772 --> 01:31:17.773
Hamish Hawks.


01:31:19.875 --> 01:31:21.076
Oh, my God.


01:31:21.276 --> 01:31:22.276
Look at this.


01:31:22.711 --> 01:31:24.179
We're almost full of surprises.


01:31:38.727 --> 01:31:39.727
What was that?


01:31:39.762 --> 01:31:40.763
I don't know.


01:31:41.396 --> 01:31:43.932
But what I do know
is we are something.


01:31:44.299 --> 01:31:45.433
We pulled it off.


01:31:45.634 --> 01:31:46.267
Yeah.


01:31:46.268 --> 01:31:47.435
That was so fun.


01:31:47.736 --> 01:31:48.770
Wasn't it fun?


01:31:48.771 --> 01:31:50.037
Well, yeah.


01:31:50.038 --> 01:31:51.807
I forgot how exciting
the whole thing can be.


01:31:51.974 --> 01:31:54.609
Yeah, well, you're not thinking of
getting back into the game, are you?


01:31:54.610 --> 01:31:56.143
No, I don't know about that.


01:31:56.144 --> 01:31:58.814
I might have had enough
excitement for now, at least.


01:31:59.114 --> 01:32:01.549
Well, that's good,
because I need an art expert


01:32:01.550 --> 01:32:03.619
to help me sell that
$100 million painting.


01:32:04.653 --> 01:32:08.924
Oh, my commission is
steep and non-negotiable.


01:32:09.124 --> 01:32:11.226
Yeah, well,
you're gonna earn every penny.


01:32:12.628 --> 01:32:13.929
Did it, guys?


01:32:14.129 --> 01:32:14.830
God, Sean.


01:32:15.130 --> 01:32:16.765
How fucking cool was that?


01:32:16.932 --> 01:32:18.767
It was so cool.


01:32:19.334 --> 01:32:20.435
Oh, man, yeah.


01:32:20.836 --> 01:32:23.170
It's all you, buddy.


01:32:23.171 --> 01:32:28.811
And I have to apologize for not buying into
this whole 4D chess thing, and I was wrong.


01:32:28.977 --> 01:32:29.644
Really?


01:32:29.645 --> 01:32:31.245
Yeah, I was wrong.


01:32:31.246 --> 01:32:33.457
Well, that's awesome, man,
because I got this other idea.


01:32:33.481 --> 01:32:35.482
Don't push it.


01:32:35.483 --> 01:32:37.829
No, no, no, I'm telling you, it's
the greatest idea for a heist ever.


01:32:37.853 --> 01:32:38.853
Wait, I want to hear it.


01:32:38.854 --> 01:32:40.022
Well, don't encourage him.


01:32:40.255 --> 01:32:41.255
No, I want to hear it.
